From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marvin Drees <marvin.drees@9elements.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon-temp: support soc64-hwmon platform device

The Intel soc64-hwmon driver exposes Agilex 5 SDM voltage and
temperature sensors via ATF SMC calls.  It registers as a platform
device, not an I2C device, so getDeviceBusAddr() returns false for
its canonical sysfs path and hwmontempsensor silently skips it.

To allow entity-manager configs to match soc64-hwmon:

1. Add a "SOC64Hwmon" entry to sensorTypes so the configuration
   daemon's type filter includes it.

2. When getDeviceBusAddr() fails, read the hwmon "name" file from the
   same directory.  If it reads "soc64hwmon" assign sentinel values
   Bus=65535 / Address=0 (matching the corresponding entity-manager
   JSON Exposes block) and continue scanning.  Any other hwmon device
   that fails getDeviceBusAddr() still hits continue as before.

3. Add #include <fstream> required for std::ifstream.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Marvin Drees <marvin.drees@9elements.com>

Note: rebased onto openbmc/dbus-sensors@dbbc389b.
The sensorTypes declaration changed from I2CDeviceTypeMap (flat_map,
entries at 4-space indent, closed with `};`) to std::to_array<>
(entries at 8-space indent, closed with 4-space `    });`).
---
 src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp b/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
index 616d0f8..24f3ea8 100644
--- a/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
+++ b/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 #include <chrono>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <filesystem>
+#include <fstream>
 #include <functional>
 #include <memory>
 #include <optional>
@@ -102,6 +103,7 @@ static constexpr auto sensorTypes =
         {"TMP468", I2CDeviceType{"tmp468", true}},
         {"TMP75", I2CDeviceType{"tmp75", true}},
         {"W83773G", I2CDeviceType{"w83773g", true}},
+        {"SOC64Hwmon", I2CDeviceType{"soc64hwmon", false}},
     });
 
 static struct SensorParams getSensorParameters(
@@ -337,7 +339,21 @@ void createSensors(
                 uint64_t addr = 0;
                 if (!getDeviceBusAddr(deviceName, bus, addr))
                 {
-                    continue;
+                    // Platform hwmon devices have no I2C bus/addr in
+                    // their canonical device path.  The soc64-hwmon SDM
+                    // sensor is one such device.  Identify it by name
+                    // and use sentinel Bus=65535/Address=0 so that
+                    // entity-manager configs with the same sentinel match.
+                    std::ifstream nameFile(directory / "name");
+                    std::string hwmonDevName;
+                    if (!nameFile.good() ||
+                        !std::getline(nameFile, hwmonDevName) ||
+                        hwmonDevName != "soc64hwmon")
+                    {
+                        continue;
+                    }
+                    bus = 65535;
+                    addr = 0;
                 }
 
                 auto thisSensorParameters = getSensorParameters(path);
-- 
